From: LuneOS <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gallivm: handle a failed execution engine instead of asserting

gallivm_compile_module() reacted to init_gallivm_engine() failing with
assert(0), and gallivm_jit_function() guarded its use of the engine with
assert(gallivm->compiled) / assert(gallivm->engine). Mesa is built with NDEBUG,
so all of those are compiled out and the failure is not handled at all:
execution fell through to

  lp_passmgr_run(..., LLVMGetExecutionEngineTargetMachine(gallivm->engine), ...)

with a NULL engine, and later to LLVMGetPointerToGlobal() on the same NULL.

Reachable whenever MCJIT creation fails - for instance running llvmpipe under
qemu-arm user-mode emulation, where LLVM cannot build an execution engine for
the emulated target:

  signal : 11 SIGSEGV (bad memory access)
  si_addr: 0x00000000
  r0     : 0x00000000
  symbol : LLVMGetExecutionEngineTargetMachine

Report the failure and leave gallivm->compiled at zero so gallivm_jit_function()
returns NULL rather than dereferencing the engine. This does not make llvmpipe
work where the JIT cannot be created - callers still have no fallback - but the
failure becomes a diagnosable error instead of a segfault in release builds.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c
index f5b6110f912..6e52e3a4cb6 100644
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/gallivm/lp_bld_init.c
@@ -412,9 +412,15 @@ gallivm_compile_module(struct gallivm_state *gallivm)
    LLVMSetDataLayout(gallivm->module, "");
    assert(!gallivm->engine);
    if (!init_gallivm_engine(gallivm)) {
-      assert(0);
+      /* Not an assert: builds define NDEBUG, so asserting here left the
+       * failure completely unhandled and the NULL engine was used a few lines
+       * below in LLVMGetExecutionEngineTargetMachine().  Leave gallivm->compiled
+       * at zero so gallivm_jit_function() refuses to hand out code.
+       */
+      _debug_printf("gallivm: failed to create an LLVM execution engine; "
+                    "cannot JIT shaders\n");
+      return;
    }
-   assert(gallivm->engine);
 
    if (gallivm->cache && gallivm->cache->data_size) {
       goto skip_cached;
@@ -512,8 +518,12 @@ gallivm_jit_function(struct gallivm_state *gallivm,
    func_pointer jit_func;
    int64_t time_begin = 0;
 
-   assert(gallivm->compiled);
-   assert(gallivm->engine);
+   /* Same reasoning as in gallivm_compile_module(): these were asserts only,
+    * which NDEBUG removes, so a failed engine reached LLVMGetPointerToGlobal().
+    */
+   if (!gallivm->compiled || !gallivm->engine) {
+      return NULL;
+   }
 
    if (gallivm_debug & GALLIVM_DEBUG_PERF)
       time_begin = os_time_get();
